From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: let apps read uids_allowed_on_restricted_networks

LineageOS declares Settings.Global.UIDS_ALLOWED_ON_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS @hide so
that the settings validator and the backup cover the key. AOSP keeps the key
only in ConnectivitySettingsManager, and a key that no Settings class declares
is readable by every app. A declared @hide key is not, so
ConnectivitySettingsManager.getUidsAllowedOnRestrictedNetworks throws a
SecurityException in an app such as the CTS network tests.

@Readable restores the AOSP behavior and keeps the validator and the backup.
---
 core/java/android/provider/Settings.java | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java b/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java
index 090c41d92bc77f745be3e42bd9ecbeff34b6450c..8b1434552e88d19a4b24f567d0ccb6474a11f45e 100644
--- a/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java
+++ b/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java
@@ -19589,6 +19589,7 @@ public final class Settings {
          *
          * @hide
          */
+        @Readable
         public static final String UIDS_ALLOWED_ON_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS =
                 "uids_allowed_on_restricted_networks";
 
